    "title": "Vanderbilt defeats Eastern Michigan in women's lacrosse with strong defensive performance - Nashville Standard",
    "text": "Shea Panzik scored her second consecutive hat trick to help Vanderbilt secure an 11-8 win over Eastern Michigan on Wednesday at the Vanderbilt Lacrosse Complex in Nashville.\nVanderbilt, now with a 3-3 record, relied on strong defense that resulted in 16 forced turnovers. This marks the highest number of turnovers forced by the team since 2020 and ties for fifth-most in program history. Chloe Bethea-Jones led the defensive effort with three caused turnovers.\nThe Commodores saw contributions from eight different scorers during the game. Freshman Gianna Frieri recorded her first career goal. Junior Avery Morton contributed both a goal and an assist, while freshman Gabby Putman matched her personal best with nine draw controls.",
    "summary": "Shea Panzik scored her second consecutive hat trick to help Vanderbilt secure an 11-8 win over Eastern Michigan on Wednesday at the Vanderbilt Lacrosse Complex in Nashville. Vanderbilt, now with a 3-3 record, relied on strong defense that resulted in 16 forced turnovers. This marks the highest number of turnovers forced by the team since 2020 and ties for fifth-most in program history. Chloe Bethea-Jones led the defensive effort with three caused turnovers. Junior Avery Morton contributed both a goal and an assist, while freshman Gabby Putman matched her personal best with nine draw controls.",
